The unconditional setting of `eseg->swp_inner_l4_offset` without checking the encapsulated L4 header type causes incorrect handling of non-TCP/UDP traffic. This leads to the software parser assuming a valid L4 header exists when it may not, resulting in improper processing of packets. Additionally, the check for `IPPROTO_UDP` is not sufficient for determining the presence of a valid L4 header.

